---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="About"
  description="Bycon builds operations software for transportation—starting with a transport management platform for NEMT and broker-led networks."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About Bycon</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      We are a software company focused on the unglamorous work that makes transportation run: scheduling, documentation,
      visibility, and data that still makes sense when an auditor asks for it.
    </p>
    <h2>What we believe</h2>
    <p>
      Moving people is different from moving packages. Trips touch health plans, members, and public programs—so
      operations need to be <strong>timely, traceable, and defensible</strong>. We build for brokers and providers who
      live in that world, especially in non-emergency medical transportation (NEMT) and similar networks.
    </p>
    <h2>What we ship</h2>
    <p>
      Our first product is a <a href="/solutions">transport management system (TMS)</a> designed for real broker and
      field workflows—not a generic map with a spreadsheet behind it. We expect to add product lines over time; when we
      do, we will keep each experience clear and purpose-built.
    </p>
    <h2>How we work with customers</h2>
    <p>
      We are hands-on with onboarding and configuration, because NEMT and broker operations do not fit a one-size
      template. If you are evaluating software for your network, <a href="/contact">get in touch</a>—we would rather
      be honest about fit than oversell.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
